{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLStartStopContinue","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The values of start, stop, and continue refer to how an element appears in musical score order, not in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"MusicXML document order. An element with a stop attribute may precede the corresponding element with a start","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute within a MusicXML document. This is particularly common in multi-staff music. For example, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stopping point for a slur may appear in staff 1 before the starting point for the slur appears in staff 2","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"later in the document.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When multiple elements with the same tag are used within the same note, their order within the MusicXML","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"document should match the musical score order. For example, a note that marks both the end of one slur and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"start of a new slur should have the incoming slur element with a type of stop precede the outgoing slur","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"element with a type of start.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStopContinue"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"The start-stop-continue type is used for an attribute of musical elements that can either start or stop, but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"also need to refer to an intermediate point in the symbol, as for complex slurs or for formatting of symbols","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"across system breaks.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","title":"Enumeration Cases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStopContinue\/continue","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStopContinue\/start","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStopContinue\/stop"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStartStopContinue\/Equatable-Implementations"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships"}],"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStartStopContinue","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL20MXLStartStopContinueO","symbolKind":"enum","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"MXLStartStopContinue","roleHeading":"Enumeration","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStartStopContinue"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstartstopcontinue"]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStartStopContinue/continue":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An intermediate point in the symbol, such as across a system break."}],"fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"`continue`","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLStartStopContinue.continue","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstartstopcontinue\/continue","ty